   "FacilityType": "import",
   "FacilityType [ref]": "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-panama-lng-gaslog/lng-shipping-firm-gaslog-strikes-tanker-deal-with-panama-power-project-idUSKCN1VP1DM",
   "Fuel": "LNG",
   "Status": "shelved",
   "Substatus": "confirmed",
   "Status [ref]": "https://asep.gob.pa/an-no-19123-elec-de-2024-04-26/, https://jusmundi.com/en/document/decision/en-sinolam-international-pte-ltd-v-republic-of-panama-party-representatives-monday-16th-march-2026, https://energynews.oedigital.com/electric-utilities/2026/01/07/panamas-sinolam-files-a-lawsuit-against-aes-and-interenergy-for-alleged-anticompetitive-conduct, https://web.archive.org/web/20250506140056/https://www.prensa.com/unidad-investigativa/isla-margarita-cronologia-de-un-despojo/, https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/sinolam-commences-icsid-arbitration-against-panama-over-cancellation-of-strategic-power-project-302718979.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com",
   "Country/Area": "Panama",
   "Researcher": "Gregor Clark",
   "LastUpdated": "2026-08-06",
   "ResearcherNotesUnit": "GC, Aug 2026: In the early months of 2026, Sinolam filed a lawsuit charging AES and InterEnergy with anti-competitive conduct, and initiated arbitration proceedings with the ICSID seeking redress for the government's cancellation of its license. While these proceedings play out, I think it makes sense to keep shelved status rather than moving to cancelled.\n\nAL2025: most likely cancelled: \"Además de PCCP, tenía el contrato para construir una planta termoeléctrica de gas natural licuado en Puerto Pilón, Colón, a través de su filial Sinolam Smarter Energy LNG Power Co. (que hasta 2018 se llamaba Martano Inc.). Aquel proyecto energético tampoco tuvo un final feliz y, el 26 de abril de 2024, la Autoridad Nacional de los Servicios Públicos (Asep) le retiró la licencia de construcción y explotación de la planta.\" See ref web-182943\nGC, Sep 2024: Presumed shelved due to lack of news in more than two years, and because the associated power plant had its license revoked by the Panamanian government in April 2024.",
   "ResearcherNotesProject": "AL2025: Part of the Gas to Power Panama project (included cc power plant). Most likely cancelled, although IGU 2025 report lists it as having begun operations in 2025. I couldn't find any evidence of that being the case, so I'm leaving it as shelved.",
